{"success": true, "message": "Test details sent successfully", "data": {"test": {"_id": "69de21ec7e39d99b57bc5aba", "analysisVideoCdn": "yt", "exam": ["605dfcb2f226ac25a8bd5fef"], "ctype": null, "position": 0, "order": 12, "enableCalculator": false, "isContinuousQuestion": false, "reattemptAvailable": false, "singleSectionMultipleSubjects": false, "timeRestricted": false, "title": "Mechanical Properties of Fluids - Test 3", "description": "Previous Year Questions as Chapter Test", "syllabus": "This test contains questions from all topics of this chapter included in the JEE Main syllabus. It includes a mix of questions from PYQs of JEE Main 2019 - 2025.", "totalTime": 50, "totalQuestions": 25, "totalMarks": 100, "bonusQuestions": null, "bonusMarks": null, "startDate": "2026-04-15T03:30:00.000Z", "endDate": "2027-04-30T00:00:00.000Z", "type": "free", "class": "605df635a37b7025c438d685", "instruction": "608289ffb160b022e9442c83", "subjects": [{"subjectId": "607018ee404ae53194e73d90", "totalMarks": 100, "bonusMarks": 0, "totalQuestions": 25, "bonusQuestions": 0, "_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d92444ee"}], "sections": [{"sectionId": {"_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d92444a5", "title": "Physics Single Correct", "sectionType": "normal", "subject": "607018ee404ae53194e73d90", "questions": [{"_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d924442f", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfab"], "topics": ["60e40fd5f1ef260f84ed1e97"], "concepts": ["60e40fd4f1ef260f84ed1e3d"], "question": {"text": "<p>Given below are two statements:</p><p>Statement I: Pressure in a reservoir of water is same at all points at the same level of water.</p><p>Statement II: The pressure applied to enclosed water is transmitted in all directions equally.</p><p>In the light of the above statements, choose the correct answer from the options given below:</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "df1238", "text": "Both Statement <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></math> and Statement <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>II</mi></math>&nbsp;are false", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d9244430"}, {"id": "91b0f6", "text": "Statement <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></math> is true but Statement <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>II</mi></math> is false", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d9244431"}, {"id": "cc26ea", "text": "Statement <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></math> is false but Statement <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>II</mi></math> is true", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d9244432"}, {"id": "f9dbee", "text": "Both Statement <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></math> and Statement <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>II</mi></math> are true", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d9244433"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d9244434", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfab"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4782"], "concepts": ["6162fafa6ed13040ec8499ce"], "question": {"text": "Water flows into a large tank with flat bottom at the rate of <math><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mi>&#160;</mi><msup><mrow><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mrow><mi>s</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>.</mo></math> Water is also leaking out of a hole of area <math><mn>1</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>c</mi><msup><mrow><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math> at its bottom. If the height of the water in the tank remains steady then this height is:"}, "options": [{"id": "96d091", "text": "<math><mn>5.1</mn><mi> </mi><mi>c</mi><mi>m</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d9244435"}, {"id": "30fdb8", "text": "<math><mn>1.7</mn><mi> </mi><mi>c</mi><mi>m</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d9244436"}, {"id": "a970cb", "text": "<math><mn>2.9</mn><mi> </mi><mi>c</mi><mi>m</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d9244437"}, {"id": "077644", "text": "<math><mn>4</mn><mi> </mi><mi>c</mi><mi>m</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d9244438"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d9244439", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfab"], "topics": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b65"], "concepts": ["60e56768499d1e49588f8ed2"], "question": {"text": "Two small drops of mercury each of radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math>&nbsp;coalesce to form a single large drop. The ratio of total surface energy before and after the change is"}, "options": [{"id": "caf234", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>2</mn><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></msup><mo>:</mo><mn>1</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d924443a"}, {"id": "806a15", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>:</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d924443b"}, {"id": "a0cf4c", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>:</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d924443c"}, {"id": "5a1673", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>:</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d924443d"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d924443e", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfab"], "topics": ["60e2fb9e66f9ce3f243b52e9"], "concepts": ["60e2fb9d66f9ce3f243b52bc"], "question": {"text": "The terminal velocity <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mfenced></math>&nbsp;of the spherical rain drop depends on the radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>r</mi></mfenced></math> of the spherical rain drop as&nbsp;"}, "options": [{"id": "90d3ed", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d924443f"}, {"id": "34cd2b", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d9244440"}, {"id": "e0ff43", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>r</mi></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d9244441"}, {"id": "f71ab1", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d9244442"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d9244443", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfab"], "topics": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b65"], "concepts": ["60e56739499d1e49588f8b51"], "question": {"text": "Given below are two statements :\nStatement I : The contact angle between a solid and a liquid is a property of the material of the solid and liquid as well.\nStatement II : The rise of a liquid in a capillary tube does not depend on the inner radius of the tube.\nIn the light of the above statements, choose the correct answer from the options given below:"}, "options": [{"id": "4133e3", "text": "Statement I is true but Statement II is false.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d9244444"}, {"id": "5de1fd", "text": "Statement I is false but Statement II is true.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d9244445"}, {"id": "7c8e95", "text": "Both Statement I and Statement II are false.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d9244446"}, {"id": "ed556c", "text": "Both Statement I and Statement II are true.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d9244447"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d9244448", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfab"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4782"], "concepts": ["60e5671a499d1e49588f87c8"], "question": {"text": "Consider a completely full cylindrical water tank of height 1.6 m and cross-sectional area $0.5 \\mathrm{~m}^2$. It has a small hole in its side at a height 90 cm from the bottom. Assume, the cross-sectional area of the hole to be negligibly small as compared to that of the water tank. If a load 50 kg is applied at the top surface of the water in the tank then the velocity of the water coming out at the instant when the hole is opened is : $\\left(\\mathrm{g}=10 \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s}^2\\right)$"}, "options": [{"id": "988544", "text": "$3 \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d9244449"}, {"id": "f86706", "text": "$5 \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d924444a"}, {"id": "8fb57b", "text": "$2 \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d924444b"}, {"id": "4ae889", "text": "$4 \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d924444c"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d924444d", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfab"], "topics": ["60e40fd5f1ef260f84ed1e97"], "concepts": ["60e40fd4f1ef260f84ed1e3d"], "question": {"text": "Consider a solid sphere of radius <math><mi>R</mi></math> and mass density <math><mi>&#961;</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mi>&#961;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mrow><mi>r</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mi>R</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mi></mi><mn>0</mn><mo>&#60;</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>&#8804;</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>.</mo></math> The minimum density of a liquid in which it will float is:"}, "options": [{"id": "beafeb", "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d924444e"}, {"id": "6ad637", "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d924444f"}, {"id": "658c4f", "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><msub><mrow><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d9244450"}, {"id": "380215", "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><msub><mrow><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d9244451"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d9244452", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfab"], "topics": ["60e2fb9e66f9ce3f243b52e9"], "concepts": ["60e2fb9d66f9ce3f243b52bc"], "question": {"text": "A small ball of mass $m$ and density $\\rho$ is dropped in a viscous liquid of density $\\rho_0$. After sometime, the ball falls with constant velocity. The viscous force on the ball is :"}, "options": [{"id": "ec2a10", "text": "$m g\\left(1-\\rho \\rho_0\\right)$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d9244453"}, {"id": "81ea86", "text": "$m g\\left(1+\\frac{\\rho}{\\rho_0}\\right)$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d9244454"}, {"id": "9e866f", "text": "$m g\\left(\\frac{\\rho_0}{\\rho}-1\\right)$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d9244455"}, {"id": "ab24f0", "text": "$m g\\left(1-\\frac{\\rho_0}{\\rho}\\right)_{\\nabla}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d9244456"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d9244457", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfab"], "topics": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b65"], "concepts": ["60e2fbdc66f9ce3f243b5648"], "question": {"text": "An air bubble of radius 0.1 cm lies at a depth of 20 cm below the free surface of a liquid of density $1000 \\mathrm{~kg} / \\mathrm{m}^3$. If the pressure inside the bubble is $2100 \\mathrm{~N} / \\mathrm{m}^2$ greater than the atmospheric pressure, then the surface tension of the liquid in SI unit is (use $\\mathrm{g}=10 \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s}^2$ )"}, "options": [{"id": "3faa47", "text": "$0.1$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d9244458"}, {"id": "56c901", "text": "$0.05$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d9244459"}, {"id": "014e8c", "text": "$0.02$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d924445a"}, {"id": "5db3d8", "text": "$0.25$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d924445b"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d924445c", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfab"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4782"], "concepts": ["60e567ab499d1e49588f95c5"], "question": {"text": "A liquid of density $\\rho$ is coming out of a hose pipe of radius a with horizontal speed $v$ and hits a mesh. $50 \\%$ of the liquid passes through the mesh unaffected. $25 \\%$ looses all of its momentum and $25 \\%$ comes back with the same speed. The resultant pressure on the mesh will be:"}, "options": [{"id": "474802", "text": "$\\frac{1}{4} \\rho v^{2}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d924445d"}, {"id": "7b4fa8", "text": "$\\frac{3}{4} \\rho v^{2}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d924445e"}, {"id": "ec926d", "text": "$\\frac{1}{2} \\rho v^{2}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d924445f"}, {"id": "eac664", "text": "$\\rho v^{2}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d9244460"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d9244461", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfab"], "topics": ["60e40fd5f1ef260f84ed1e97"], "concepts": ["60e40fd4f1ef260f84ed1e3d"], "question": {"text": "An air bubble of volume <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>cm</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;rises from the bottom of a lake <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>40</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> deep to the surface at a temperature of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>12</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>.</mo></math> The atmospheric pressure is &nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>5</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Pa</mi><mo>,</mo></math> the density of water is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1000</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>.</mo><mo>&#160;</mo></math>There is no difference of the temperature of water at the depth of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>40</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> and on the surface. The volume of air bubble when it reaches the surface will be"}, "options": [{"id": "a3d039", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>cm</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d9244462"}, {"id": "b20a2c", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>cm</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d9244463"}, {"id": "bb03d7", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>cm</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d9244464"}, {"id": "98edc5", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>cm</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d9244465"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d9244466", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfab"], "topics": ["60e2fb9e66f9ce3f243b52e9"], "concepts": ["60e2fb9d66f9ce3f243b52bc"], "question": {"text": "<p>A water drop of radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mi>&#956;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> falls in a situation where the effect of buoyant force is negligible. Co-efficient of viscosity of air is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math> and its density is negligible as compared to that of water <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>6</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></math>. Terminal velocity of the water drop is</p><p>(Take acceleration due to gravity <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>)</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "dc599e", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>145</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d9244467"}, {"id": "7c9616", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>123</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d9244468"}, {"id": "a7ca11", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>118</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d9244469"}, {"id": "1e6d11", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>132</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d924446a"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d924446b", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfab"], "topics": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b65"], "concepts": ["6117b5e3478ae845c43c5e11"], "question": {"text": "A air bubble of radius <math><mrow><mn>1</mn><mtext>&#160;cm</mtext></mrow></math> in water has an upward acceleration of <math><mrow><mn>9.8</mn><msup><mrow><mtext>&#160;cms</mtext></mrow><mrow><mo>&#8211;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></math>. The density of water is <math><mrow><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow><mtext>&#160;gm&#160;cm</mtext></mrow><mrow><mo>&#8211;</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></math> and water offers negligible drag force on the bubble. The mass of the bubble is <math><mrow><mfenced><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>980</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>cm</mtext><mo>/</mo><msup><mtext>s</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced></mrow></math>."}, "options": [{"id": "4d9a1a", "text": "<math><mrow><mn>4.51</mn><mtext>&#160;gm</mtext></mrow></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d924446c"}, {"id": "3e63de", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>15</mn><mtext>&#160;gm</mtext></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d924446d"}, {"id": "0a5917", "text": "<math><mrow><mn>4.15</mn><mtext>&#160;gm</mtext></mrow></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d924446e"}, {"id": "1747e2", "text": "<math><mrow><mn>1.52</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>gm</mtext></mrow></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d924446f"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d9244470", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfab"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4782"], "concepts": ["61ada03cdedd066c316e55c8"], "question": {"text": "Given below are two statements:\nStatement I : When speed of liquid is zero everywhere, pressure difference at any two points depends on equation $P_1-P_2=\\rho g\\left(h_2-h_1\\right)$.\nStatement II : In ventury tube shown $2 \\mathrm{gh}=v_1^2-v_2^2$\n<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2FdxXCTxmiK1SJfsVkDZuRoShBJNreZBvtBmhcOlnWRdM.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\"><br />In the light of the above statements, choose the most appropriate answer from the options given below."}, "options": [{"id": "fef01b", "text": "Both Statement I and Statement II are correct.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d9244471"}, {"id": "301d99", "text": "Statement I is correct but Statement II is incorrect.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d9244472"}, {"id": "75c729", "text": "Statement I is incorrect but Statement II is correct.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d9244473"}, {"id": "175fbb", "text": "Both Statement I and Statement II are incorrect.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d9244474"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d9244475", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfab"], "topics": ["60e40fd5f1ef260f84ed1e97"], "concepts": ["60e40fd4f1ef260f84ed1e3d"], "question": {"text": "A glass tumbler having inner depth of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>17</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> is kept on a table. A student starts pouring water <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#956;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math> into it while looking at the surface of water from the above. When he feels that the tumbler is half filled, he stops pouring water. Up to what height, the tumbler is actually filled ?"}, "options": [{"id": "d950de", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d9244476"}, {"id": "3af452", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>11</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d9244477"}, {"id": "3a663f", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>7</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d9244478"}, {"id": "726902", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>75</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d9244479"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d924447a", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfab"], "topics": ["60e2fb9e66f9ce3f243b52e9"], "concepts": ["60e2fb9d66f9ce3f243b52bc"], "question": {"text": "In an experiment to verify Stokes law, a small spherical ball of radius&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi></math> and density <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#961;</mi></math> falls under gravity through a distance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>h</mi></math> in air before entering a tank of water. If the terminal velocity of the ball inside water is same as its velocity just before entering the water surface, then the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>h</mi></math> is proportional to: (ignore viscosity of air)"}, "options": [{"id": "817b75", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d924447b"}, {"id": "a6b18c", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d924447c"}, {"id": "2e8593", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d924447d"}, {"id": "a322c4", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d924447e"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d924447f", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfab"], "topics": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b65"], "concepts": ["6162fafc6ed13040ec849b61"], "question": {"text": "<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F5791be83-8183-4fe5-8d60-ca23bb8707aa.png?alt=media\" /><br />Two liquids of densities <math><msub><mrow><mi>&#961;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math> and <math><msub><mrow><mi>&#961;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>&#961;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mrow><mi>&#961;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfenced></math> are filled up behind a square wall of side <math><mn>10</mn><mi></mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> as shown in figure. Each liquid has a height of <math><mn>5</mn><mi></mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>.</mo></math> The ratio of the forces due to these liquids exerted on upper part MN to that at the lower part NO is (Assume that the liquids are not mixing):"}, "options": [{"id": "fa961a", "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d9244480"}, {"id": "27a8f8", "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d9244481"}, {"id": "a046a1", "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d9244482"}, {"id": "f12102", "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d9244483"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d9244484", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfab"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4782"], "concepts": ["6162fafa6ed13040ec8499ce"], "question": {"text": "<p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2Fa528e366-fdce-4841-b6ea-3e4d9f760505.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 400px; height: 150px;\" /></p><p>The figure shows a liquid of given density flowing steadily in horizontal tube of varying cross-section. Cross-sectional areas at&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>&nbsp;is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>cm</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>25</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>mm</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>,</mo></math> if the speed of liquid at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>60</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>&#8211;</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></math> is</p><p>(Given&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>P</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></math>&nbsp;are liquid pressures at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> points.</p><p>Density&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#961;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1000</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;are on the axis of tube)</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "e8dcd8", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>135</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>P</mi><mi>a</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d9244485"}, {"id": "cb21c8", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>27</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>P</mi><mi>a</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d9244486"}, {"id": "92eabd", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>175</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>P</mi><mi>a</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d9244487"}, {"id": "f383e1", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>36</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>P</mi><mi>a</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d9244488"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d9244489", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfab"], "topics": ["60e40fd5f1ef260f84ed1e97"], "concepts": ["60e40fd4f1ef260f84ed1e3d"], "question": {"text": "A submarine experiences a pressure of <math><mn>5.05</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></math> at a depth of <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math> in a sea. When it goes further to a depth of <math><mi>&#160;</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> , it experiences a pressure of <math><mi>&#160;</mi><mn>8.08</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></math> . Then <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math> is approximately (density of water <math><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></math> and acceleration due to gravity <math><mi>&#160;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math> ):"}, "options": [{"id": "65d089", "text": "<math><mn>600</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d924448a"}, {"id": "81d195", "text": "<math><mn>500</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d924448b"}, {"id": "cb7f82", "text": "<math><mn>300</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d924448c"}, {"id": "d3a360", "text": "<math><mn>400</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d924448d"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d924448e", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfab"], "topics": ["60e2fb9e66f9ce3f243b52e9"], "concepts": ["60e2fb9d66f9ce3f243b52bc"], "question": {"text": "A spherical ball of radius $1 \\times 10^{-4} \\mathrm{~m}$ and density $10^5 \\mathrm{~kg} / \\mathrm{m}^3$ falls freely under gravity through a distance $h$ before entering a tank of water, If after entering in water the velocity of the ball does not change, then the value of $h$ is approximately:\n(The coefficient of viscosity of water is $9.8 \\times 10^{-6} \\mathrm{~N} \\mathrm{~s} / \\mathrm{m}^2$ )"}, "options": [{"id": "e0ab5e", "text": "$2296 \\mathrm{~m}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d924448f"}, {"id": "23a3ec", "text": "$2518 \\mathrm{~m}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d9244490"}, {"id": "90c20f", "text": "$2249 \\mathrm{~m}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d9244491"}, {"id": "e9c080", "text": "$2396 \\mathrm{~m}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d9244492"}], "questionLabels": []}], "markingScheme": {"_id": "608283e223cf4b3ad8f125e6", "title": "JEE Single Correct", "correctAttempt": 4, "incorrectAttempt": -1, "createdAt": "2021-04-09T08:45:27.797Z", "updatedAt": "2021-07-05T05:39:15.785Z", "__v": 0, "updated_by": "6042252509c5bf34e8a2f178"}, "maximumAttemptLimit": 20, "linkedQuestions": [], "createdAt": "2026-04-14T14:28:54.475Z", "updatedAt": "2026-04-14T14:28:54.475Z", "__v": 0}, "position": 0, "_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d92444ec"}, {"sectionId": {"_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d92444ea", "title": "Physics Numerical", "sectionType": "normal", "subject": "607018ee404ae53194e73d90", "questions": [{"_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d92444ce", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfab"], "topics": ["60e567de499d1e49588f9cd5"], "concepts": ["60e567fa499d1e49588fa01c"], "question": {"text": "A hydraulic press can lift <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math> when a mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math>&nbsp;is placed on the smaller piston. It can lift kg when the diameter of the larger piston is increased by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math> times and that of the smaller piston is decreased by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math> times keeping the same mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math>&nbsp;on the smaller piston."}, "options": [{"id": "0bb6d5", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d92444cf"}, {"id": "1d6e06", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d92444d0"}, {"id": "339543", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d92444d1"}, {"id": "36e890", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d92444d2"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d92444d3", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfab"], "topics": ["60e2fb5766f9ce3f243b4f37"], "concepts": ["60c9e848ea076dc381c0df47"], "question": {"text": "A vessel with square cross-section and height of 6 m is vertically partitioned. A small window of $100 \\mathrm{~cm}^2$ with hinged door is fitted at a depth of 3 m in the partition wall. One part of the vessel is filled completely with water and the other side is filled with the liquid having density $1.5 \\times 10^3 \\mathrm{~kg} / \\mathrm{m}^3$. What force one needs to apply on the hinged door so that it does not get opened ?<br/>(Acceleration due to gravity $=10 \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s}^2$)"}, "options": [{"id": "b62207", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d92444d4"}, {"id": "58eb09", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d92444d5"}, {"id": "fefbcf", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d92444d6"}, {"id": "2ca240", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d92444d7"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d92444d8", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfab"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4782"], "concepts": ["60e5671a499d1e49588f87c8"], "question": {"text": "<p>Glycerin of density <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>25</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>&#8211;</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></math> is flowing through the conical section of pipe. The area of cross-section of the pipe at its ends are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>cm</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math> and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>cm</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;and pressure drop across its length is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>&#8211;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>. The rate of flow of glycerine through the pipe is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>&#8211;</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>&#8211;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> is _____.</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "ea5c4b", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d92444d9"}, {"id": "7b995b", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d92444da"}, {"id": "b70388", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d92444db"}, {"id": "6e7ce8", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d92444dc"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d92444dd", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfab"], "topics": ["6117b89167dbe2603c3e818e"], "concepts": ["6117b88f67dbe2603c3e80b0"], "question": {"text": "<p>The area of cross-section of a large tank is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></math>. It has a narrow opening near the bottom having area of cross-section <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></math>. A load of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>25</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math> is applied on the water at the top in the tank. Neglecting the speed of water in the tank, the velocity of the water, coming out of the opening at the time when the height of water level in the tank is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>40</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> above the bottom, will be _____&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>cm</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>.</p><p>[Take <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math> ]</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "c7d279", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d92444de"}, {"id": "65396e", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d92444df"}, {"id": "d90cc0", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d92444e0"}, {"id": "4ff34b", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d92444e1"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d92444e2", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfab"], "topics": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b65"], "concepts": ["60e2fbdc66f9ce3f243b5648"], "question": {"text": "A liquid column of height $0.04 \\mathrm{~cm}$ balances excess pressure of a soap bubble of certain radius. If density of liquid is $8 \\times 10^3 \\mathrm{~kg} \\mathrm{~m}^{-3}$ and surface tension of soap solution is $0.28 \\mathrm{Nm}^{-1}$, then diameter of the soap bubble is _____ $\\mathrm{cm}$. (if $g=10 \\mathrm{~m} \\mathrm{~s}^{-2}$ )"}, "options": [{"id": "3cec2d", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d92444e3"}, {"id": "f1ceb2", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d92444e4"}, {"id": "683c1e", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d92444e5"}, {"id": "53ddc4", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d92444e6"}], "questionLabels": []}], "markingScheme": {"_id": "608283c623cf4b3ad8f125e5", "title": "JEE Numerical", "correctAttempt": 4, "incorrectAttempt": -1, "createdAt": "2021-04-09T08:45:27.797Z", "updatedAt": "2021-07-05T05:39:27.056Z", "__v": 0, "updated_by": "6042252509c5bf34e8a2f178"}, "maximumAttemptLimit": 5, "linkedQuestions": [], "createdAt": "2026-04-14T14:28:54.555Z", "updatedAt": "2026-04-14T14:28:54.555Z", "__v": 0}, "position": 1, "_id": "69de4f262ee0e063d92444ed"}], 